---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Figure from "@/components/Figure.astro";
import DotChart from "@/components/DotChart.astro";
import { ARMS, SUMMARY_BY_ID, deskTasks, buildTasks, processTasks, processCampaign, PROCESS_PILOT, provenance, findings, intervals, deskComparison, deskCampaign, DESK_CAMPAIGN, REPO, SITE, ORG, AUTHORS, RELEASE, REPS, fmt, taskBootstrap } from "@/lib/data";
const desk = deskTasks(), build = buildTasks(), proc = processTasks(), pilot = processCampaign(PROCESS_PILOT);
const F = Object.fromEntries(ARMS.map((a) => [a.id, findings(a.id)]));
const I = Object.fromEntries(ARMS.map((a) => [a.id, intervals(a.id)]));
const comparison = deskComparison(), bs = provenance().paired_task_bootstrap;
const attemptsTotal = ARMS.reduce((n, a) => n + SUMMARY_BY_ID[a.id].attempts, 0);
const dc = deskCampaign(DESK_CAMPAIGN), dcRank = [...dc.arms].sort((a, b) => dc.summary[b.id].passed - dc.summary[a.id].passed);
const count = (k: number) => ["no", "one", "two", "three", "four", "five", "six"][k] ?? String(k);
const dcPair = dc.pair ? dc.pair.arms.map((id) => dc.arms.find((a) => a.id === id)!) : [];
const desc = `Business Bench tests AI agents on everyday business work: ${desk.length} public tasks such as reconciling spreadsheets, preparing imports and writing reports, each checked automatically.`;
// Latest results: per system, share of attempts accepted and share of tasks accepted every time, with 95% ranges over tasks.
const latest = dcRank.map((a) => {
  const perTask = desk.map((t) => dc.matrix[t.id][a.id]);
  const frac = perTask.map((rs: any[]) => rs.filter((r: any) => r.passed).length / rs.length);
  const all = perTask.map((rs: any[]) => (rs.every((r: any) => r.passed) ? 1 : 0));
  const mean = (xs: number[]) => xs.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / xs.length;
  return { a, s: dc.summary[a.id], rate: mean(frac), rateCi: taskBootstrap(frac), all: mean(all), allCi: taskBootstrap(all) };
});
const plainName: Record<string, string> = { "proto-sol6-sub": "Proto on GPT-6 sol", "codex-sol6": "Codex on GPT-6 sol", "proto-deepseek-direct": "Proto on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash" };
const gap = dc.pair!.difference_percentage_points, gapCi = dc.pair!.bootstrap_95_percent_interval_pp;
const pts = (x: number) => `${x >= 0 ? "+" : "−"}${Math.abs(x).toFixed(1)}`;
const cite = `@misc{businessbench2026,
  title        = {Business Bench: Evaluating Agents on Business Deliverables},
  author       = {${AUTHORS.map((a) => { const p = a.split(" "); return `${p.slice(1).join(" ")}, ${p[0]}`; }).join(" and ")}},
  year         = {2026},
  howpublished = {\\url{${SITE}}},
  note         = {Version ${RELEASE.version}}
}`;
const jsonld = [
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite", name: "Business Bench", url: SITE + "/", publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: ORG.name, url: ORG.url } },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Dataset", name: "Business Bench desk comparison", url: SITE + "/results", description: desc,
    version: RELEASE.version, datePublished: RELEASE.date, isAccessibleForFree: true, license: `${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`,
    creator: [{ "@type": "Organization", name: ORG.name, url: ORG.url }],
    variableMeasured: ["attempt acceptance", "all-three acceptance", "required-check completion", "wall time", "captured model cost"],
    distribution: [{ "@type": "DataDownload", encodingFormat: "application/x-ndjson", contentUrl: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/erphq/business-bench/main/results/latest/attempts.jsonl` }],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Business Bench" description={desc} path="/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <nav slot="contents" class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <span class="toc-h">On this page</span>
    <a href="#latest">Latest results</a><a href="#what">What is tested</a><a href="#how">How answers are checked</a>
    <a href="#earlier">Earlier results</a><a href="#caveats">Keep in mind</a><a href="#evidence">Check it yourself</a><a href="#cite">Cite</a>
  </nav>
  <h1>Business Bench</h1>
  <p class="meta">Public tasks, automatic checks and every recorded attempt<span class="sep">·</span>MIT licence</p>
  <p class="lede">Business Bench tests AI agents on everyday business work: reconciling spreadsheets, preparing files for import, writing reports and handling routine finance tasks. Each task comes with its input files and a set of automatic checks, and an answer counts only if it passes all of them.</p>
  <p class="byline">{AUTHORS.join(", ")} · {ORG.name} Research</p>
  <div class="article-links"><a href={`/results/${dc.label}`}>See the latest results</a><a href="/tasks">Browse the tasks</a><a href="/paper">Read the paper</a></div>

  <h2 id="latest">Latest results</h2>
  <p>We gave three AI agent setups all {desk.length} tasks, three times each, and checked every answer with the same rules. Proto is the agent built by {ORG.name}; Codex is OpenAI’s coding agent. Two of the setups use the same underlying model, GPT-6 sol, so the difference between them comes from the agent itself.</p>
  <Figure n={1} id="figure-1">
    <DotChart
      label={latest.map((r) => `${plainName[r.a.id] ?? r.a.system}: ${fmt.pct(r.rate)} of answers accepted, ${fmt.pct(r.all)} of tasks accepted all three times`).join("; ")}
      domain={[0.6, 1]} ticks={[0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1]}
      keys={[{ label: "Answers accepted", shape: "" }, { label: "Tasks accepted all three times", shape: "ring" }]}
      rows={latest.map((r) => ({
        label: plainName[r.a.id] ?? r.a.system, sub: `${r.s.passed} of ${r.s.attempts} answers`, slot: r.a.slot,
        points: [
          { value: r.rate, lo: r.rateCi[0], hi: r.rateCi[1], title: `Answers accepted ${fmt.pct(r.rate)}` },
          { value: r.all, lo: r.allCi[0], hi: r.allCi[1], shape: "ring", title: `Accepted all three times ${fmt.pct(r.all)}` },
        ], valueText: fmt.pct(r.rate), valueSub: `every time ${fmt.pct(r.all)}`,
      }))}
    />
    <Fragment slot="caption">Results from {dc.date}. The lines show the range the result could plausibly fall in on a similar set of tasks (95% range). <a href={`/results/${dc.label}`}>Full results, task by task</a>.</Fragment>
  </Figure>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Proto and Codex on the same model are close.</strong> Proto got {Math.abs(gap).toFixed(1)} points {gap >= 0 ? "more" : "fewer"} answers accepted, but the plausible range runs from {pts(gapCi[0])} to {pts(gapCi[1])}, so neither is clearly better on these tasks.</li>
    <li><strong>Proto on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash did as well as either.</strong> It also took the least time per task.</li>
    <li><strong>Getting it right every time is harder.</strong> Each setup solved roughly four in five tasks on all three tries; the rest were solved only some of the time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="what">What is tested</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Kind of task</th><th>What the agent does</th><th>Results so far</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><a href="/tasks#desk"><b>File tasks</b></a><br />{desk.length} tasks</td><td>Gets a folder of business files and a short request, and produces the finished files: a reconciled workbook, an import file, a summary report.</td><td><a href={`/results/${dc.label}`}>Latest results</a> and <a href="/results">earlier results</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/tasks#build"><b>App building</b></a><br />{build.length} tasks</td><td>Builds a small internal business app, then makes three changes to it.</td><td>Tasks published; no scores yet.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/process"><b>Working inside an ERP</b></a><br />{proc.length} tasks</td><td>Takes a job such as a buyer or accounts clerk inside a business system for several simulated days.</td><td><a href="/process#campaign">Early pilot</a> on {pilot.tasks.length} tasks.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2 id="how">How answers are checked</h2>
  <p>A report can look finished and still be wrong: a balanced workbook may leave out a customer, and a correct payment may break an approval rule. So each task lists exactly what a correct answer must contain, and a program checks it: the right rows, the right numbers, formulas that recalculate, and the facts a written summary has to mention. An answer is accepted only if every check passes. The tasks and the checks are public, so anyone can see what was asked and dispute a check.</p>

  <h2 id="earlier">Earlier results</h2>
  <p>On 16 September we compared Proto on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash with Codex on GPT-5.6 sol over the same tasks, three times each. Proto got {SUMMARY_BY_ID["proto-deepseek"].passed} of {SUMMARY_BY_ID["proto-deepseek"].attempts} answers accepted and Codex {SUMMARY_BY_ID["codex-sol"].passed}. Those two setups used different models, so that comparison mixes the agent and the model. <a href="/results">See the earlier results</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="caveats">Keep in mind</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>{ORG.name} builds Proto and runs this benchmark. The tasks, checks and every recorded answer are public so others can check the results; the <a href="/audit">audit page</a> lists what can and cannot be verified.</li>
    <li>The tasks were available while Proto was being developed, so these results say how the agents do on these tasks, not on work they have never seen.</li>
    <li>Passing most checks is common; passing all of them is harder. The <a href="/analysis">findings</a> page shows how close the failed answers came.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="evidence">Check it yourself</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>If you want to know</th><th>Start here</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>What an agent was asked to do</td><td><a href="/tasks/payments-match-v2">An example task</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Whether the numbers add up</td><td><a href="/reproduce">Verify the results</a> without running any agent</td></tr>
      <tr><td>How it was measured</td><td><a href="/methods">Methods</a> and <a href="/paper">the paper</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>How to run it on your own agent</td><td><a href={`${REPO}#run-the-benchmark-with-proto`} rel="noopener">Instructions on GitHub</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2 id="cite">Cite</h2>
  <pre class="cite" aria-label="BibTeX citation">{cite}</pre>
  <p class="muted">Found a problem with a task or a check? <a href={`${REPO}/issues`} rel="noopener">Report it on GitHub</a> with the task name.</p>
</Base>
